After some work here it is: my first 'quick' and 'low score' ascension.
With a Caveman (ooops, sorry, Cavewoman :-), ascended with 742212 points
after 28025 moves. She was level 23 with 183 HP when ascended (not as wimpy
as some earlier posters, but I didn't try to opimise for that ;-)

I must say, that playing for fast, low score ascension was a real fun - I had
to develop a completely different strategy then I was used to. The usefulness
of various items/intrinsics also changed a lot - e.g. one of the key items for
me were jumping boots... (jump over the monster and run - killing him takes 
time and increases score). Of course you don't collect gold or gems, don't
waste time on dead branches like Ludios, don't polypile (takes lot of time to
collect there piles together and to examine the results)... Of the demon
lords I killed only Juiblex (had no choice - he swallowed me), plus let the
Orcus kill himself. The others I just escaped.

I did not really use all the 'speed-up' tricks I can think of (e.g. used that
confused gold detection trick only once on the elemental planes, the rest of
the portals I honestly located, with a little help from the AoY). I also made 
some stupid mistakes that costed extra time. Plus I'm not sure if Caveman is 
really the best character for fast ascension - it just so happened that I've 
choosen "C". So it looks for me, that an ascension in 20000 moves should be 
feasible. Good Luck ;-)
